<%#
  Step Outline — the whole list as a tree: the trunk from the start step as
  sibling nodes at level 1 (each node renders its own exits), then the steps
  nothing leads to.

  The tree role lives here, not on #steps-list: that element also holds the
  empty state (buttons, template cards), and a tree may own only treeitems
  and groups. Most re-renders replace #steps-list's CHILDREN, so a role on it
  would not follow the list between empty and not.

  The Unconnected section is a group labelled by its heading, so its trees
  are level 2 and their exits one deeper.

  Local variables: workflow, outline (StepOutline::Result).
%>
<div class="builder__outline" role="tree" aria-label="Steps">
  <% node = outline.root %>
  <% while node %>
    <%= render "workflows/step_node", node: node, workflow: workflow, outline: outline, level: 1 %>
    <% node = node.continuation&.kind == :step ? node.continuation.child : nil %>
  <% end %>
  <% if outline.orphan_roots.any? %>
    <div class="builder__outline-unconnected" role="group" aria-labelledby="steps-unconnected-heading">
      <div class="builder__outline-section" id="steps-unconnected-heading">Unconnected: nothing leads here yet</div>
      <%# Each unconnected tree renders like the main one: its trunk as
          siblings, its exits nested, its stubs growable. %>
      <% outline.orphan_roots.each do |orphan| %>
        <% node = orphan %>
        <% while node %>
          <%= render "workflows/step_node", node: node, workflow: workflow, outline: outline, level: 2 %>
          <% node = node.continuation&.kind == :step ? node.continuation.child : nil %>
        <% end %>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  <% end %>
</div>
